From c97670f0131487e777d86598816123ee76c02140 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 23:28:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] test: qualify internal helpers so tests run outside the
 package namespace

testSimulationFunctions.R and test-legacy-actuarial.R called unexported
functions (.fAxn, .fAExn, ..., axyznvect) without lifecontingencies:::.
They passed under test_check() and devtools::test(), which evaluate tests
in the package namespace, but failed with test_file()/test_dir() on the
installed package.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Bc6gsUsDwi4tAJ4wArX8fC
---
 tests/testthat/test-legacy-actuarial.R   |  2 +-
 tests/testthat/testSimulationFunctions.R | 20 ++++++++++----------
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tests/testthat/test-legacy-actuarial.R b/tests/testthat/test-legacy-actuarial.R
index 410b4de..cff4555 100644
--- a/tests/testthat/test-legacy-actuarial.R
+++ b/tests/testthat/test-legacy-actuarial.R
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@ test_that("multiple-table annuity vectorization agrees with scalar implementatio
                           x = x, lx = Ix, name = "SOA2008"))
   tables <- list(tab, tab, tab)
   result <- sapply(10:90, function(y) {
-    axyznvect(tables, x = c(y, y + 1, y + 2)) ==
+    lifecontingencies:::axyznvect(tables, x = c(y, y + 1, y + 2)) ==
       axyzn(tables, x = c(y, y + 1, y + 2))
   })
   expect_true(all(result))
